--- task
id: t27
dataset: section8
kind: lexical ranking

--- intent
Rank documents by the BM25 relevance of their body to the text `$q`; return the top 10 titles with the score as `s`.

--- params
{"q": "graph databases"}

--- edition2
query about($q: String) {
  match { $d: Doc }
  return { $d.title, bm25($d.body, $q) as s }
  order { bm25($d.body, $q) desc }
  limit 10
}

--- edition3 disputed
query about($q: String) {
  match { from bm25({ match { $d: Doc } return { $d } }, $d.body, $q) as $score }
  return { $d.title, $score as s }
  order { $score desc }
  limit 10
}

--- expect ordered
columns: ["d.title","s"]
["The graph primer",2.0232522]
["Rust in production",1.0116261]
["The graph of cities",0.9156194]

--- note
Disputed on #1316 at a1b89621 (the 2026-11-19 M0 re-run): the edition-3 text is accepted and returns the recorded documents in the recorded order, but `bm25` scores are F64 there while the rows recorded from edition 2 hold F32 scores (2.0232521362860822 against 2.0232522), so its rows differ from the recorded rows by value. The rows are not edited; the text is kept as `edition3 disputed`, not a truth.
